    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d508">

                <pb facs="0957" n="833" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg833"/>

                <head>No. 504.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Señor de
                        Zamacona.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-07-05"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 5,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 6th ultimo, relative to the complaint of the Mexican
                    Government regarding cattle-stealing from Mexico by bands of thieves domiciled
                    in Texas, and to inform you that this Department will do all that lies within
                    its power towards checking these thefts.</p>
                <p>To that end I have addressed both the Secretary of the Interior and the governor
                    of the State of Texas in the matter, furnishing them with copies of your note,
                    and requesting that such measures as may lie within their respective
                    jurisdictions may be promptly and energetically adopted to correct and prevent
                    any abuses which may be found to exist.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES G. BLAINE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
